---
title: "One Month, Two Shocks"
subtitle: "What 547,271 US flights from January 2024 say about delays and cancellations"
author: "Zhiyang Cheng"
date: last-modified
date-format: "MMMM YYYY"
---



::: {.lead-text}
January 2024 looks like an ordinary winter month at first. But when I loaded every domestic
flight into a MySQL database on AWS and asked it questions, two separate disruptions
stood out: a wave of winter storms, and the grounding of one aircraft type that hit two
airlines especially hard. This page tells that story. The
[7 SQL questions](questions.qmd) page gives the exact queries and answers.
:::

